# Settings of the metacheck Docker installation. The installer writes them to
# the file .env next to compose.yaml; change a line there and start metacheck
# again (docker compose up) to change it. Without any of them, metacheck is
# the lightest installation: PDFs go to TU/e's GROBID server, and the power
# check runs without a language model.

# GROBID on this computer (about 4 GB of memory more), so PDFs stay here:
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=grobid
# GROBID_LOCAL_URL=http://grobid:8070
# METACHECK_GROBID_URL=http://grobid:8070

# The language model of the power check, either Ollama on this computer ...
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# METACHECK_LLM_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b
# ... or Mistral (EU) with your own API key (https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys);
# the paragraphs about statistical power are then sent to Mistral:
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# Where this file is, shown by the app when it explains how to add a key:
# METACHECK_SETTINGS_FILE=
